{
  "$meta": {
    "name": "Akwaaba",
    "version": "0.2.0",
    "concept": "Akwaaba is Twi for welcome, and this product's job is to hand somebody the keys to a place they trust. The system is built for photographs of buildings: ink chrome so images sit in a frame rather than float on grey, warm ivory ground so daylight reads as daylight, and one gold accent because restraint is what makes an accent mean something. Type carries the voice - a serif with real character against a neutral UI sans, because a product whose headings and body are the same face has no face at all.",
    "constraints": [
      "Readable in direct sun on a 300-nit phone: body contrast targets 7:1, never below 4.5:1.",
      "Primary action is ink, not a hue. It cannot fail contrast, and it leaves the accent free to actually accent.",
      "Touch targets 48dp, Android's minimum, not iOS's 44.",
      "Two families, both self-hosted through next/font. Elevation is warm-tinted and shallow; animation stays on transform and opacity so a 2019 Android device never composites layout."
    ]
  },
